[%# The mobile drawer's contents.

    WHY THIS EXISTS. global_header.tt has always had a drawer and a hamburger button,
    but its body was `[% IF mobile_navigation %][% mobile_navigation %][% END %]` and no
    controller ever set `mobile_navigation`, so the drawer was permanently empty. This
    partial is that missing half, INCLUDEd rather than passed in as a variable: the
    drawer's contents are a presentation concern and no controller needs to know about it.

    WHAT IT CARRIES. The top-level sections, which global_header.css hides below 768px -
    without these the four sections are unreachable on a phone.

    WHAT IT DOES NOT CARRY, DELIBERATELY. The contextual tree is NOT rendered here. The
    obvious implementation - emitting `nav_html` a second time - costs about 875KB of
    markup on this site, because that tree is 1310 items: it took content pages from
    910KB to 1.8MB and the splash page, which shows no sidebar at all, from 46KB to
    920KB. So `#mobile-nav-tree` below is an empty socket, and lib/navigation.ts MOVES the
    single rendered tree out of the desktop sidebar into it below 768px, returning it
    above. One copy in the document, no duplicated ids, no added page weight, and the
    expand/collapse handlers travel with the element because they are bound to it.

    The section list is deliberately NOT .spectrum-SideNav: @spectrum-css/sidenav is not
    a dependency of this site. It reuses the .nav-item + spectrum-Link + spectrum-Heading
    combination the desktop header already uses, so the two navigations stay visually
    consistent without pulling in a package for one list.
-%]
[% mobile_sections = ['Harrypedia', 'Fan Fiction', 'Searches', 'Bookmarks'] -%]
<ul class="mobile-nav-sections">
  [% FOREACH section IN mobile_sections -%]
    <li class="nav-item">
      [%# "Fan Fiction" contains a space and is emitted raw, matching the desktop header
          in global_header.tt. Browsers encode it on the way out and this has never
          caused trouble, so the readable form wins over a literal %20 in the output. -%]
      <a href="/[% section %]" class="spectrum-Link spectrum-Link--primary spectrum-Link--quiet">
        <span class="spectrum-Heading spectrum-Heading--serif spectrum-Heading--sizeXS">
          [% section %]
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
  [% END -%]
</ul>

[%# Hidden until navigation.ts moves a tree in, so pages without a sidebar show no
    stray separator. -%]
<div class="mobile-nav-tree-section" id="mobile-nav-tree-section" hidden>
  <hr role="separator" class="spectrum-Divider spectrum-Divider--sizeM" />
  <div class="mobile-nav-tree" id="mobile-nav-tree"></div>
</div>
